<%#
  The What's New frequency picker, on its own so two surfaces can share it
  (issue #1061).

  Extracted from `global-common-updates.ejs`, which still renders it in place on
  the What's New tab. The Getting Started page renders it too, because the whole
  point of #995 — absorbed into #1061 — is asking this once, up front, rather
  than leaving it to be found after it has already interrupted somebody.

  One definition rather than two: the option list and the `default` must match
  `DEFAULT_CHANGELOG_NOTIFICATION_POLICY` in `version-check.ts`, and a copy on a
  second page is a copy that drifts the next time that default moves.
%>
<sdpi-item label="What's New page">
  <sdpi-select setting="changelogNotification" default="never" global>
    <option value="always">Open after every update</option>
    <option value="features">Only after updates with new features</option>
    <option value="monthly">Open at most once a month</option>
    <option value="never">Never open</option>
  </sdpi-select>
</sdpi-item>
